  "resources": [
    "S3 bucket: nebula-audit-covered-012345678901_1",
    "S3 bucket: nebula-audit-uncovered-a-012345678901_1",
    "Lambda function: nebula-audit-fn-a",
    "DynamoDB table: nebula-audit-table"
  ],
  "timeframe": "current configuration as of 2026-11-05T13:28:43Z",
  "criteria": "For each resource, determine whether CloudTrail data event logging is actually ON today. Check: 1) list all trails via use_aws cloudtrail list_trails/describe_trails, 2) for each trail get_event_selectors to see classic data event selectors (S3/Lambda/DynamoDB resource types, specific ARNs vs account-wide/all-S3-buckets wildcard), 3) check for advanced event selectors with field-level filters (eventCategory=Data, resources.type, resources.ARN matching or not matching specific ARNs), 4) note if logging is All/ReadOnly/WriteOnly and whether trail is actually logging (is_logging). Determine effective coverage per resource - e.g. a trail covering 'all S3 buckets' would cover both S3 buckets even if only one is explicitly named; an exclude-pattern or specific ARN list might exclude one. Report clearly per-resource: COVERED or NOT COVERED, and which trail/selector causes that result."
}"}, "type": "tool_use"}], "created_at": null}

